_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.39574858997571116,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.19131814530989205,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.80033994,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"SS Innovations International, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a commercial-stage surgical robotics company in India, Philippines, Indonesia, South America, Iraq, Cyprus, Oman, United Arab Emirates (UAE), Nepal, and internationally. It offers SSi Mantra, a surgical robotic system; and SSi Mudra, a range of stapling, energy, and core instrumentations for surgical systems. The company also develops NADI \u0096 Automated Coronary Anastomotic Connector, a micro stapling device; SSi Multi-Fire Clip Applier, a cartridge-based clip applicator; SSi Robotic Stapler; SSi Maya is an enabling digital platform that compliments the SSI Mantra system and enhances surgical capabilities; SSi Guru is a virtual tele illustration; SSi XR Cognitive Skill Simulator is an extended reality (XR) software platform developed to train and educate surgeons and surgical assistants; SSi MantraM; SSi Mantra Tele Surgeon Console (TSC); and 5mm surgical instruments; SSi Holographic Anatomy, an augmented reality tool; SSi Chitrasa \u0096 Advanced DICOM Viewer, an AI enabled application viewer; and SSi Mixed Reality Headset, a medical-grade device. In addition, it offers instrument tips, including forceps, scissors, electrocautery tools, scalpels, and other surgical tools. Further, the company provides accessory products, such as sterile drapes, 3d stereo endoscopes, cannulas, and seals, as well as tele proctoring and telesurgery products. Additionally, it offers installation, repair, maintenance, 24/7 technical support, and proactive health monitoring services. The company sells its products through direct sales organizations and distributor networks. SS Innovations International, Inc. is headquartered in Gurugram, India.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Sudhir Prem Srivastava M.D. | Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 77 | Compensation: $899,538 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 483 people. Revenue per employee of $88K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $17K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["SS Innovations International In is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $255M market cap on $42M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +106% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -189% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 43%.","The company is burning through $22M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +8.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -7.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 19% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 80% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +8.6% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 255% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (67% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $2.2M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the mar